  <releases>
    <release version="0.1.60" date="2026-08-19" urgency="medium">
      <description>
        <p>A command line that works without a display, repository switching without a restart, and dates read from the document instead of guessed.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>New command line: miaz search finds documents in any repository and miaz repos lists them, so searching works over SSH and in scripts</li>
          <li>Switch repository without restarting the application, and choose separately whether it becomes the default</li>
          <li>The filing date is read from the document itself: PDF creation date, XMP, image EXIF and Office metadata, with no extra libraries needed</li>
          <li>A date that cannot be read is filed as 99991231 and sorts to the end, instead of being silently filed under today</li>
          <li>Ambiguous dates such as 03/04/2024 are refused rather than guessed, and document metadata is trusted over digits in a filename</li>
          <li>The rename dialog has a button to read the date again on demand</li>
          <li>Plugins unload completely and start clean, which fixes a crash on right click after disabling a plugin</li>
          <li>The projects file can no longer be emptied when the app and the workspace disagree about which repository is open</li>
          <li>Faster, quieter startup: the plugin directories are scanned once instead of twice, and the browser page no longer reloads once per plugin</li>
          <li>First automated interface test suite, plus a manual checklist used as the release gate</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.50" date="2026-08-12" urgency="medium">
      <description>
        <p>Groundwork release: the workspace filter, the document index and the configuration each became a thing of their own, and both packages are now verified before release.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The document parse moved into a new index, so it exists once instead of twice and can be tested without a display</li>
          <li>The workspace filter became a value that can be saved, restored and compared, which is what saved searches will need</li>
          <li>Each repository owns its configuration, so switching no longer reads settings left behind by the previous one</li>
          <li>Background work runs through one helper that reports its failures, instead of eight hand-rolled threads that swallowed them</li>
          <li>A failed background operation no longer freezes the workspace for the rest of the session</li>
          <li>Plugins can contribute sidebar and header bar widgets through helpers that clean up after themselves on unload</li>
          <li>The rename dialog refuses to apply a name that is not valid, and gained a Manage projects button</li>
          <li>The .deb and the .rpm are built from one export of one commit and checked against distribution policy before release</li>
          <li>Fixed the "Since last year" date filter, which covered the wrong period</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.40" date="2026-08-05" urgency="medium">
      <description>
        <p>Secrets in the system keyring, a localized interface, a faster workspace, and a rename dialog plugins can extend.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>AI provider API keys are stored in the system keyring instead of plain text</li>
          <li>Country, Group and Purpose labels are shown in your language; French and German catalogues added</li>
          <li>Plugins can add tabs to the rename dialog: set a project or a periodicity while renaming</li>
          <li>Rename dialog is keyboard-friendly: typeable date, Ctrl+Enter to apply, Esc to cancel, invalid names refused</li>
          <li>Faster workspace on large repositories: single file changes update one row, and scans no longer touch the disk per row</li>
          <li>New MiAZInsights plugin page: all-years overview, period selector, activity heatmap, rank movers and a world map</li>
          <li>One AI plugin: MiAZAIChat merged into MiAZAIAssistant, so providers are configured once</li>
          <li>Adding documents is always available: it moved from an optional plugin into the app</li>
          <li>Optional third-party libraries install into a private virtualenv, never into the system Python</li>
          <li>Failed plugins are reported in the app instead of only the log, and every plugin now has an icon</li>
          <li>Config files are written atomically, so a crash cannot leave a half-written repository</li>
          <li>Fixed date filters that hid documents at month boundaries and past midnight</li>
          <li>Flatpak packaging is deprecated: a sandboxed build cannot reach host tools such as ocrmypdf and scanimage</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.30" date="2026-07-08" urgency="medium">
      <description>
        <p>See CHANGELOG.md for details.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.29" date="2026-07-06" urgency="medium">
      <description>
        <p>See CHANGELOG.md for details.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.28" date="2026-06-27" urgency="medium">
      <description>
        <p>AI chat, mass rename as a core feature, a per-repository change journal, and several new plugins.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>New plugin MiAZAIChat: chat about a document via Claude, OpenAI, Gemini, or Ollama</li>
          <li>Mass rename is now a core feature with a guided Concept transform dialog</li>
          <li>Per-repository change journal records every add, rename, and delete with import provenance</li>
          <li>New plugins: MiAZNewspaper, MiAZYearReport, MiAZOCR, MiAZFullscreen, MiAZColumnVisibility</li>
          <li>MiAZNotes renders the note body as Markdown in view mode</li>
          <li>Embedded localhost web server with a built-in Browser page</li>
          <li>Global crash handling with a log file and an error dialog</li>
          <li>Rename: filenames forced to uppercase, and Suggest metadata from documents sharing the concept</li>
          <li>Sidebar filters: case-insensitive substring search with sorted entries</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.26" date="2026-05-16" urgency="medium">
      <description>
        <p>AI-assisted renaming, document notes, column visibility, and rename dialog improvements.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>New plugin MiAZAIAssistant: propose all seven filename fields via Claude, OpenAI, Gemini, or Ollama</li>
          <li>New plugin MiAZNotes: attach Markdown notes to any document with faceted filtering and backup/restore</li>
          <li>New plugin MiAZColumnVisibility: toggle workspace column visibility</li>
          <li>Rename dialog: inline Add buttons on restricted-vocabulary rows</li>
          <li>Rename dialog: Concept autocomplete via difflib-backed popover</li>
          <li>Workspace: Adw.InlineViewSwitcher for workspace view switching</li>
          <li>Backend: filename_guess_date() probes PDF metadata, EXIF, and file mtime</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.25" date="2026-05-05" urgency="medium">
      <description>
        <p>Sidebar redesign, unified plugin system, performance improvements and startup fixes.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Sidebar rebuilt with Adw.Sidebar (icon-only filter rows and resizable pane)</li>
          <li>Plugin system unified: no more system/user distinction</li>
          <li>Plugin sidebar filters now show the plugin icon</li>
          <li>Review button turns red when pending documents exist</li>
          <li>Eliminated spurious workspace updates on startup</li>
          <li>Dropdowns now show "Any country", "Any group", etc.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.8" date="2025-07-21" urgency="low" />
    <release version="0.1.7" date="2025-03-22" urgency="low" />
    <release version="0.0.48" date="2024-07-12" urgency="low" />
  </releases>
</component>
